  <name>Nomm</name>
  <summary>Modern Linux-First Mod Manager</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      NOMM is a stupid simple, super clean &quot;native&quot; (as in it runs on Linux without having to use translation tools...) mod manager for Linux. The goal here is to keep the setup really simple for users like me who don&apos;t need the super advanced/complex features. Just a few clicks on a clean, modern interface, and you&apos;re done :)
    </p>
    <p>
      Don&apos;t expect NOMM to manage mods for something like Skyrim. There are specific tools for that (see NaK or Jackify).
    </p>
    <p>
      Instead, think of NOMM as more of a general purpose tool for most games that just need you to point to a directory and extract some mod archives.
    </p>
  </description>
